# Idle skip with shell writes the firmware reads (tools/check-idle-skip.sh),
# on configs/test-idle-blx-wild-nrf52840.yaml: its loop polls a SysTick
# count at 0x20000100 until it reaches 20, then branches through r3.  While
# the loop is being skipped, the shell points r3 at main instead of
# 0xFFFFFFFF and then sets the count to 20 between two ticks: the loop must
# leave on its next read, not at the next SysTick, and the firmware starts
# over (a second "S", a second loop, then the wild branch).  A write that
# did not drop the proof would let the skip run on (the tripwire aborts).
#   ./build/test_runner test configs/test-idle-blx-wild-nrf52840.yaml --script test/scripts/idle-skip-shell-writes.cnsh
every 3ms reg 1 pc
at 33ms reg 1 r3 = 0x105
at 55ms mem -w 1 0x20000100 = 20
at 55ms mem -w 1 0x20000100 1
at 300ms reg 1 pc
